   "variant_id": null,
   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "A function \\( f \\) has derivatives of all orders. The third-degree Taylor polynomial for \\( f \\) about \\( x = -1 \\) is used to approximate \\( f\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\). It is known that \\( f^{(4)}(-1) = 16 \\) and that \\( |f^{(4)}(x)| \\le 48 \\) for all \\( x \\) between \\( -1 \\) and \\( - \\frac{1}{2} \\). Find the Lagrange error bound for this approximation."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         1,
         8
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "A degree 3 polynomial needs the maximum of \\( |f^{(4)}(x)| \\), the derivative of order \\( 4 \\), between the centre and the input.",
         "mathjson": 4
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The bound is \\( \\frac{M\\,|x - -1|^{4}}{4!} \\) with \\( M = 48 \\) and \\( |x - -1| = \\frac{1}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            8
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Evaluating gives \\( \\frac{48 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{4}}{24} = \\frac{1}{8} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            8
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The error is at most \\( \\frac{1}{8} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            8
         ]
      }
   ],
